 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to the imposition of sales and compensating use taxes in the county of Jefferson",
    "basePrintNo": "S5171",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5171-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5171\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the tax law, in relation to the\nimposition of sales and compensating use taxes in the county of\nJefferson\n\nPURPOSE: Authorizes County of Jefferson to extend the current rate of\nsales and compensating use taxes for the period beginning September 1,\n2004 and ending November 30, 2017.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the tax law to authorize and empower the county of\nJefferson to adopt and amend local laws, ordinances, or resolution to\ncontinue to impose a one percent additional tax rate during the period\nof September 1, 2004 and ending November 30, 2017.\n\nSection 2 provides the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: Currently, 54 out of 57 counties, exclusive of the City\nof New York, have sales tax rates in excess of 3% and, therefore, must\nask for special legislation to continue these additional rates.\nJefferson County's extender would place it alongside 40 other counties\nthat currently are authorized to impose an additional one percent\nsales and compensating use tax.\n\nSince the county began collecting the additional tax they have been\nable to lower their property tax rate significantly. However, the\ncounty now faces major capital costs, including a new radio system and\nassistance to Jefferson Community College. Jefferson County has also\nhad to hire ten additional corrections officers as a result of a\nrecent state analysis to increasing personnel and to staff a newly\nconstructed jail dormitory. These costs, along with ever-rising\nmandated spending, necessitate an increase in the sales tax rate\n\nSince the implementation of the additional local sales tax program in\n2004 the Jefferson County has responsibly insured that the funds were\nused wisely and to help control costs for the benefit of all county\nresidents. They will continue to do so with this extension of the\nsales and compensating use taxes.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately,\n\n",
